lesson: 211
title: Teeth of grown-ups and children
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A young child with all the first teeth, the milk teeth, has 20 of them.
explain: A grown-up with all the teeth has 32, because the adult teeth are more and bigger than the milk teeth.
explain: To count the teeth of a family, count the grown-ups' teeth and the children's teeth and add them.
explain: 2 grown-ups and 3 young children: 2 × 32 = 64 and 3 × 20 = 60, so 64 + 60 = 124 teeth.
vars: a=name g=2..5 c=2..6 z=3..9
answer: g * 32 + c * 20
exercise: A dentist checks {g} grown-ups and {c} young children. All of them have all their teeth, and the children still have all their milk teeth. How many teeth does the dentist count?
exercise: {a}'s family has {g} grown-ups and {c} young children, each with a full set of teeth. How many teeth do they have altogether?
exercise: At a school check-up the nurse looks at the teeth of {c} young children with all their milk teeth and {g} teachers with all their teeth. How many teeth does the nurse look at?
exercise: How many teeth do {g} grown-ups and {c} small children have in all, if nobody has lost a tooth?
exercise: {g} parents and {c} toddlers brush their teeth at bedtime. Every one of them has a full set. How many teeth get brushed?
exercise: A toothpaste advert shows {g} smiling grown-ups and {c} smiling little kids, all with a full set of teeth. How many teeth are in the advert?
exercise: {g} grownups n {c} little kids all with all their teeth. how many teeth is that lol
exercise: dentist today, me n my sibs — {c} of us little ones, all milk teeth still in — plus {g} grownups. how many teeth did she count
exercise: {a} reckons a grown-up has 20 teeth like a kid. nah. {g} grown-ups and {c} kids, full sets, how many teeth altogether?
exercise: {g+1} adults — no wait, {g} adults, and {c} wee ones, everyone's got all their teeth. total teeth?
exercise: waiting room had {z} magazines and like {g} grown-ups and {c} toddlers, all full sets of teeth. how many teeth in the room
test: Every person in a group of {g} grown-ups and {c} young children still has all of their teeth. What is the total number of teeth in the group?
test: All their teeth are there: {c} children with milk teeth and {g} adults. Find how many teeth there are.
test: {a} counts the teeth in the family photo: {g} grown-ups and {c} little ones are smiling, no gaps anywhere. How many teeth could {a.he} count?
test: The tooth fairy has not yet visited any of {c} small children, and their {g} parents have every tooth. How many teeth do they have between them?
test: {c} kids n {g} adults, nobody lost a tooth yet. teeth?
test: {c} of us little kids — oh and {g} grownups. all full sets. how many teeth we got
test: {g} grown-ups, {z} chairs and {c} young children are in the dentist's waiting room. Everyone has a complete set of teeth. How many teeth are there?
exam: Given that a party comprises {g} adults and {c} young children, each possessing a complete dentition, determine the aggregate number of teeth.
exam: It is stated that no member of a household of {g} adults and {c} infants of pre-school age has lost a tooth. Ascertain the total number of teeth in the household.
exam: Compute the cardinality of the set of teeth belonging to {g.words} adult persons and {c.words} young children, all dentitions being complete.
exam: Pursuant to an inspection of {g} adults and {c} children with full primary dentition, state the number of teeth examined.
exercise: Last year {g+1} grown-ups and {c} young children went to the dentist together. Grandad has since passed away, and this year all the others go. Everyone has a full set of teeth, the children all their milk teeth. How many teeth does the dentist count this year?
exercise: there was {g+1} grownups in our house till great-uncle Bert kicked the bucket, now it's just the rest of em plus {c} little kids. full sets of teeth all round. how many teeth, come on it ain't hard
test: {a} stretched the truth a bit and told the class there are {g+3} grown-ups in {a.his} house. Really there are {g} grown-ups and {c} young children, all with every tooth. How many teeth are in the house?
